Capsule root: `<capsule>`. Every capsule-relative path (`artifacts/…`, `runtime-state/…`, `workflows/…`, `repos/…`) resolves against this root, NEVER against your current working directory — a `cd` can persist across your shell calls. Read and write them by absolute path: `artifacts/<name>` means `<capsule>/artifacts/<name>`.

Raw downloads (CI artifacts, traces, screenshots and video bundles) go under `artifacts/downloads/`, which the capsule chain never commits; `artifacts/` keeps conclusions and small excerpts. A file over 16 MiB elsewhere is left out of the chain too and listed in `artifacts/oversize.json`.

This dispatch runs on pi, whose sub-agents do not run with this step's isolation: a worker the `subagent` tool starts loads the context files, skills and prompt templates this step was started without. Dispatch no sub-agent: do the analysis and build every unit yourself, record each unit's `implemented_by` in `artifacts/build/units.json` as `main`, and say in your hand-off that this harness offers no isolated sub-agent.

# Prohibited actions

Unless your step definition explicitly requires it, never:

- read or write the daemon's data or config: `$POLYFORGE_DATA_DIR` (else `~/.local/share/polyforge`), `~/.config/polyforge`, and the directories `$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` and `$PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` name (running `pf` is fine);
- create or change a `.claude/settings*.json`, a Claude Code or git hook, or a command-running key in any git config, `--global` and `--system` included (`core.fsmonitor`, `core.hooksPath`, `core.sshCommand`, an alias, a filter);
- read or write another work item's capsule or worktree, or a workspace file outside `<capsule>`;
- kill or signal a process you did not start.

